<overview>
<p>Capellan infantry serve where BattleMechs and armor cannot be spared, which in the resource-constrained CCAF means nearly everywhere. The Xin Sheng movement revitalized the infantry arm alongside every other facet of the Capellan Confederation Armed Forces, giving foot soldiers better equipment and renewed purpose. Jump-capable infantry give CCAF commanders a vertical mobility option for urban combat and rough terrain operations. The added cost of jump equipment limits their numbers compared to foot formations, but their ability to bypass obstacles and reach elevated positions makes them valuable in the defensive fighting the Confederation often faces. Light David gauss rifle sections carry precision electromagnetic weapons that deliver exceptional accuracy and penetration at range, making these platoons a serious threat to lightly armored targets.</p>
</overview>

<notes>
Intro date based on production date of David Light Gauss Rifle. Striker Carbine is standard CCAF long arm.
</notes>

